    course_description = '<p>This course will prepare you for careers in the fields of information technology, IT management and cyber security.<br/></p><p>In your first year, you’ll be introduced to concepts including programming, mathematics, networking, databases and computer security. You’ll then develop advanced skills in IT that include web development, data management and visualisation in an enterprise context, IT security management and project management. You’ll also tackle complex IT projects – either with peers or on your own.<br/></p><p>This course has been accredited by ECU as an <a href="https://www.aqf.edu.au/framework/aqf-qualifications">AQF Level 7 Bachelor Degree<i></i></a> Award.</p><p>70 Indicative ATAR</p><p>ECU admission and English language requirements apply.</p><p>See <a href="#courseEntryDom">Course Entry</a> for further information.</p><p><a href="https://www.ecu.edu.au/study/shared-content/admission-information-sets/U67.pdf">Course admission profile</a> <p><a href="https://www.ecu.edu.au/study/shared-content/admission-information-sets/Whole-of-Institution-Information-Set.pdf">ECU admission profile</a></p> </p><p><a href="https://www.ecu.edu.au/study/shared-content/admission-information-sets/Whole-of-Institution-Information-Set.pdf">ECU admission profile</a></p>',
