UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Journalism drives democracy and shapes social change, and broadcast media brings these stories to life across TV, radio, online, and social platforms.<br/></p><p>In this course you’ll gain hands-on skills that extend beyond traditional reporting. You will learn to engage audiences on issues that matter including social justice, climate change, diversity, and inclusivity, across all media channels.<br/> The Bachelor of Journalism and Broadcast Media focuses on news, entertainment, and sports reporting, and presenting. You’ll also learn about the business side of journalism, including how to monetise content for a successful freelance career.<br/></p><p>This course has been accredited by ECU as an <a href="https://www.aqf.edu.au/framework/aqf-qualifications">AQF Level 7 Bachelor Degree<i></i></a> Award.</p><p>70 Indicative ATAR</p><p>ECU admission and English language requirements apply.</p><p>See <a href="#courseEntryDom">Course Entry</a> for further information.</p><p><a href="https://www.ecu.edu.au/study/shared-content/admission-information-sets/H31.pdf">Course admission profile</a> <p><a href="https://www.ecu.edu.au/study/shared-content/admission-information-sets/Whole-of-Institution-Information-Set.pdf">ECU admission profile</a></p> </p><p><a href="https://www.ecu.edu.au/study/shared-content/admission-information-sets/Whole-of-Institution-Information-Set.pdf">ECU admission profile</a></p>',
