UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Thinking of studying Law? Start your journey at ECU.<br/> Our fully accredited Law degree is designed to fit around your life, available both on-campus and online, so you can balance study with your other commitments.<br/></p><p>More than just legal theory, our Law Program builds the practical skills you''ll need in the courtroom and beyond, opening doors to diverse careers in legal practice, business, government, and social justice. At ECU, students gain hands-on advocacy experience through mooting competitions and have the rare opportunity to cross-examine WA Police officers as part of their training.<br/> Thanks to our partnership with the Northern Suburbs Community Legal Centre, students also work on real legal matters, applying their knowledge in authentic settings and developing the confidence and competence needed for a successful legal career.<br/> Whether you aspire to be a lawyer, legislator, or champion of human rights, ECU equips you with the expertise, opportunities, and support to make it happen. Law at ECU isn’t just a course – it is your launchpad.<br/></p><p>This course has been accredited by ECU as an <a href="https://www.aqf.edu.au/framework/aqf-qualifications">AQF Level 7 Bachelor Degree<i></i></a> Award.</p><p>85 Indicative ATAR</p><p>ECU admission and English language requirements apply.</p><p>See <a href="#courseEntryDom">Course Entry</a> for further information.</p><p><a href="https://www.ecu.edu.au/study/shared-content/admission-information-sets/V72.pdf">Course admission profile</a> <p><a href="https://www.ecu.edu.au/study/shared-content/admission-information-sets/Whole-of-Institution-Information-Set.pdf">ECU admission profile</a></p> </p><p><a href="https://www.ecu.edu.au/study/shared-content/admission-information-sets/Whole-of-Institution-Information-Set.pdf">ECU admission profile</a></p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 208,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 69600,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
