UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>This course is a perfect entry point to studying aviation if you’re working in the industry or fly as a hobby.<br/></p><p>It also provides a pathway into the Bachelor of Aviation course where you can graduate with a bachelor level program with an additional two years of study using credits for the units you’ve already completed.<br/> This on-campus course provides a focused, professional education and graduate status for those seeking to enter the aviation industry. The course is technically oriented, covering a good breadth of the underlying science and technology related to aircraft systems in addition to a range of more general content areas related to the aviation industry.<br/></p><p>This course has been accredited by ECU as an <a href="https://www.aqf.edu.au/framework/aqf-qualifications">AQF Level 5 Diploma<i></i></a> Award.</p><p>ECU admission and English language requirements apply.</p><p>See <a href="#courseEntryDom">Course Entry</a> for further information.</p><p><a href="https://www.ecu.edu.au/study/shared-content/admission-information-sets/W88.pdf">Course admission profile</a> <p><a href="https://www.ecu.edu.au/study/shared-content/admission-information-sets/Whole-of-Institution-Information-Set.pdf">ECU admission profile</a></p> </p><p><a href="https://www.ecu.edu.au/study/shared-content/admission-information-sets/Whole-of-Institution-Information-Set.pdf">ECU admission profile</a></p><p>Commonwealth supported - estimated 1st year indicative fee <strong>AUD $8,950</strong></p>',
