    course_description = '<p>Do you have a degree in health, counselling, social work, occupational therapy, nursing, midwifery or a psychology related subject?<br/></p><p>Maybe you have worked in mental health for at least five years? Whatever your experience, this course provides a pathway to becoming a specialist mental health nurse. This course will develop your skills in assessment and intervention strategies applicable to a variety of mental health settings.<br/></p><p>This course has been accredited by ECU as an <a href="https://www.aqf.edu.au/framework/aqf-qualifications">AQF Level 8 Graduate Certificate<i></i></a> Award.</p><p>ECU admission and English language requirements apply.</p><p>See <a href="#courseEntryDom">Course Entry</a> for further information.</p><p><a href="https://www.ecu.edu.au/study/shared-content/admission-information-sets/Whole-of-Institution-Information-Set.pdf">ECU admission profile</a></p><p>Commonwealth supported - estimated 1st year indicative fee <strong>AUD $2,400</strong></p><p>See <a href="#feesScholarshipsDom">Fees and Scholarships</a> for further information.</p>',
