-- ⏭️ (no CRICOS): Graduate Diploma of Creative Writing Online | https://www.ecu.edu.au/degrees/courses/graduate-diploma-in-creative-writing-accelerated-online

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Are you an aspiring early childhood teacher with an existing degree?<br/></p><p>This course will equip you to teach in early childhood settings after one year of full-time study. Focusing specifically on children from birth to five years of age, this course is centred on the care and education of children in this age group in partnership with families and communities.<br/> This course is built on the principle that students come to the program with strengths from a diverse range of educational and life experiences. Reflective thinking and research, with an emphasis on links between theory and practice is valued. Students develop a deep understanding of the importance of building strong, positive relationships with children, families, communities and colleagues. Students are taught how to develop, implement and assess socially inclusive curricula where children are valued, respected and productively engaged in learning.<br/> This course accommodates "principles and dimensions" of excellence and is delivered through mutually beneficial partnerships between ECU, and individual schools and early childhood settings.<br/></p><p>This course has been accredited by ECU as an <a href="https://www.aqf.edu.au/framework/aqf-qualifications">AQF Level 8 Graduate Diploma<i></i></a> Award.</p><p>ECU admission and English language requirements apply.</p><p>See <a href="#courseEntryDom">Course Entry</a> for further information.</p><p><a href="https://www.ecu.edu.au/study/shared-content/admission-information-sets/Whole-of-Institution-Information-Set.pdf">ECU admission profile</a></p><p>Commonwealth supported - estimated 1st year indicative fee <strong>AUD $4,750</strong></p><p>See <a href="#feesScholarshipsDom">Fees and Scholarships</a> for further information.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 52,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 4750,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<p>Admission requirements you''ll need to meet for this course.</p><ul> <li> <p>Academic admission requirements (Band 6) may be satisfied through completion of one of the following:</p><ul> <li>Bachelor degree; or</li> <li>Equivalent prior learning including at least five years relevant professional experience.</li></ul><br/> </li> <li> <p>International students must attain an IELTS Academic with an average level of 7.0 or more, across the four components of listening, speaking, reading and writing; no score below level 6.5 in any of these components; and a score of 7.0 or more in the components of speaking and listening. Note: IELTS Academic One Skill Retake will also be considered. Internationally schooled applicants may also be required to meet this requirement.</p> <p>English competency requirements may also be satisfied through completion of one of the following:</p> <ul> <li>Bachelor degree or master degree from Australia, Canada, Ireland, New Zealand, the UK or the USA, or</li> <li>Undergraduate degree taught in English from a South African University.</li> </ul> </li> </ul><p>Academic admission requirements (Band 6) may be satisfied through completion of one of the following:</p><ul> <li>Bachelor degree; or</li> <li>Equivalent prior learning including at least five years relevant professional experience.</li></ul><p>International students must attain an IELTS Academic with an average level of 7.0 or more, across the four components of listening, speaking, reading and writing; no score below level 6.5 in any of these components; and a score of 7.0 or more in the components of speaking and listening. Note: IELTS Academic One Skill Retake will also be considered. Internationally schooled applicants may also be required to meet this requirement.</p><p>English competency requirements may also be satisfied through completion of one of the following:</p><ul> <li>Bachelor degree or master degree from Australia, Canada, Ireland, New Zealand, the UK or the USA, or</li> <li>Undergraduate degree taught in English from a South African University.</li> </ul><p>Admission requirements you''ll need to meet for this course.</p><ul> <li> <p>Academic admission requirements (Band 6) may be satisfied through completion of one of the following:</p><ul> <li>Bachelor degree; or</li> <li>Equivalent prior learning including at least five years relevant professional experience.</li></ul><br/> </li> <li> <p>International students must attain an IELTS Academic with an average level of 7.0 or more, across the four components of listening, speaking, reading and writing; no score below level 6.5 in any of these components; and a score of 7.0 or more in the components of speaking and listening. Note: IELTS Academic One Skill Retake will also be considered. Internationally schooled applicants may also be required to meet this requirement.</p> <p>English competency requirements may also be satisfied through completion of one of the following:</p> <ul> <li>Bachelor degree or master degree from Australia, Canada, Ireland, New Zealand, the UK or the USA, or</li> <li>Undergraduate degree taught in English from a South African University.</li> </ul> </li> </ul><p>Academic admission requirements (Band 6) may be satisfied through completion of one of the following:</p><ul> <li>Bachelor degree; or</li> <li>Equivalent prior learning including at least five years relevant professional experience.</li></ul><p>International students must attain an IELTS Academic with an average level of 7.0 or more, across the four components of listening, speaking, reading and writing; no score below level 6.5 in any of these components; and a score of 7.0 or more in the components of speaking and listening. Note: IELTS Academic One Skill Retake will also be considered. Internationally schooled applicants may also be required to meet this requirement.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.ecu.edu.au/degrees/courses/graduate-diploma-in-early-childhood-teaching',
    updated_at = NOW()
